        ('90030017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b', 'What were the three estates in 18th-century French society? Which estate paid all the taxes?', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Social Science', 'The French Revolution', 2, 'The three estates were: First Estate (Clergy), Second Estate (Nobility), and Third Estate (Big businessmen, merchants, court officials, lawyers, peasants, and landless artisans). Only the Third Estate paid all direct and indirect taxes (Taille and Tithe).', '1 Mark for listing the 3 estates correctly; 1 Mark for specifying that the Third Estate bore all taxes', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c', 'What is the ''Preamble'' to the Indian Constitution? State any two core democratic values enshrined in it.', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Social Science', 'Constitutional Design', 2, 'The Preamble is an introductory guiding statement that sets out the guiding purposes, principles, and philosophy of the Constitution. Core values: Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, Republic, Justice, Liberty, Equality, and Fraternity (any two).', '1 Mark for definition of Preamble; 1 Mark for mentioning two core values with brief context', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d', 'Explain any three major demands made by Vladimir Lenin in his famous ''April Theses'' of 1917.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Socialism in Europe and the Russian Revolution', 3, 'In April 1917, Bolshevik leader Vladimir Lenin returned to Russia and put forward three urgent demands known as April Theses: 1. The ongoing First World War must be brought to an immediate close. 2. All land owned by the nobility and clergy must be transferred to the peasants. 3. All banks must be nationalized under state control.', '1 Mark for end of World War I; 1 Mark for transfer of land to peasants; 1 Mark for nationalization of banks', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e', 'Describe the three Himalayan river systems that form the northern plains of India and state two characteristics of their drainage.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Drainage', 3, 'The three river systems are: 1. The Indus River System, 2. The Ganga River System, 3. The Brahmaputra River System. Characteristics: (i) They are perennial rivers fed by both rainfall and melting Himalayan snow. (ii) In their upper courses, they perform intensive erosional action forming deep gorges, while in lower courses they create floodplains, meanders, and expansive deltas.', '1 Mark for naming the three river systems; 2 Marks for two distinct hydrological characteristics (perennial flow and depositional landforms)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000f', 'Why is an independent and impartial judiciary essential in a constitutional democracy like India?', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Constitutional Design', 3, 'An independent judiciary is vital because: 1. Protector of Fundamental Rights: Citizens can approach courts (High Courts and Supreme Court) under Articles 32 and 226 if rights are infringed. 2. Guardian of the Constitution: It has the power of Judicial Review to strike down unconstitutional executive orders and parliamentary laws. 3. Dispute Resolution: It resolves legal disputes between center and states or between citizens and the state impartially.', '1 Mark for protection of Fundamental Rights; 1 Mark for Judicial Review; 1 Mark for federal dispute settlement', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030017-0000-4000-8000-000000000010', '(a) What were the primary social, economic, and political causes of the French Revolution of 1789? (b) How did the Declaration of the Rights of Man and Citizen transform French society?', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'Social Science', 'The French Revolution', 5, '(a) Causes: 1. Political: Autocratic rule of Louis XVI, administrative corruption, and financial bankruptcy due to involvement in American Revolutionary War. 2. Social: Division into three estates where privileged first two estates enjoyed tax exemptions, while the third estate was oppressed. 3. Economic: Population explosion, crop failures, and rising price of bread causing subsistence crises. (b) Transformational impact: The Declaration established equality before the law, freedom of speech and press, religious toleration, and popular sovereignty, replacing divine right monarchy with the ideals of Liberty, Equality, and Fraternity.', '3 Marks for analyzing political, social, and economic causes; 2 Marks for evaluating the Declaration of the Rights of Man', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030017-0000-4000-8000-000000000011', '(a) Explain any three major powers of the Prime Minister of India. (b) Why is the Council of Ministers collectively responsible to the Lok Sabha?', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'Social Science', 'What is Democracy? Why Democracy?', 5, '(a) Powers of the Prime Minister: 1. Leader of the Government: Presides over Cabinet meetings, coordinates work of departments, and makes major national policy decisions. 2. Allocation of Portfolios: Advises the President on appointing ministers and allocates or redistributes departmental portfolios. 3. Link to President: Serves as the chief communicator between the Council of Ministers and the President of India. (b) Collective Responsibility: Under Article 75(3), all ministers sink and swim together. If a Vote of No-Confidence is passed against the Prime Minister or Government in the Lok Sabha, the entire Council of Ministers must resign immediately, ensuring democratic accountability to the elected representatives.', '3 Marks for three distinct powers of Prime Minister; 2 Marks for constitutional mechanism of collective responsibility', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030017-0000-4000-8000-000000000012', 'Refer to the text and answer: (i) How was the Peninsular Plateau of India formed? (ii) Name the two broad divisions of the Peninsular Plateau separated by the Narmada river. (iii) Why is the peninsular plateau of immense economic importance to India?', NULL, NULL, 'CASE', 'Social Science', 'Physical Features of India', 4, '(i) The Peninsular Plateau was formed due to the breaking and drifting of the ancient Gondwana supercontinent, making it one of the oldest and most stable landmasses on Earth. (ii) The two divisions are: Central Highlands (north of the Narmada) and Deccan Plateau (south of the Narmada). (iii) Economic importance: 1. Storehouse of minerals: Contains huge reserves of iron ore, coal, bauxite, and mica. 2. Black soil (regur) in Deccan trap ideal for cotton cultivation. 3. Waterfall sites provide immense hydroelectric potential.', '1 Mark for Gondwana origin; 1 Mark for Central Highlands & Deccan Plateau; 2 Marks for minerals, black soil, and economic significance', 'India is endowed with diverse physical relief features resulting from tectonic plate movements. The peninsular plateau is an ancient landmass formed by breaking and drifting of the Gondwana continent. It consists of two broad divisions: the Central Highlands and the Deccan Plateau. The plateau is rich in valuable mineral deposits like iron ore, coal, and bauxite, while its black cotton soil (regur) supports prolific agriculture.', NULL, 'MEDIUM', true)
