        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-000000000002', 'Who was the leader of the Bolshevik party in Russia during the 1917 October Revolution?', '{"A":"Karl Marx","B":"Vladimir Lenin","C":"Joseph Stalin","D":"Leon Trotsky"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'Social Science', 'Socialism in Europe and the Russian Revolution', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Vladimir Lenin returned from exile and led the Bolsheviks to overthrow the Provisional Government in October 1917.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-000000000003', 'The infamous ''Enabling Act'' passed on 3rd March 1933 in Germany allowed Hitler to:', '{"A":"Declare war on Britain","B":"Establish dictatorship and rule by decree without parliament","C":"Abolish the Nazi party","D":"Form the Weimar Republic"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'Social Science', 'Nazism and the Rise of Hitler', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Enabling Act suspended civil liberties, bypassed the Reichstag, and established Hitler''s dictatorial totalitarian rule.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-000000000004', 'The Standard Meridian of India (82°30'' E) passes through which of the following cities in Uttar Pradesh?', '{"A":"Mirzapur","B":"Lucknow","C":"Kanpur","D":"Varanasi"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'MCQ', 'Social Science', 'India - Size and Location', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The 82°30'' E longitude passing through Mirzapur (near Prayagraj) is adopted as the Indian Standard Time (IST) meridian.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-000000000005', 'Which parallel of latitude divides India into almost two equal halves?', '{"A":"Equator","B":"Tropic of Cancer (23°30'' N)","C":"Tropic of Capricorn (23°30'' S)","D":"Arctic Circle"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'Social Science', 'India - Size and Location', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Tropic of Cancer at 23°30'' N latitude passes through eight Indian states, dividing the country into subtropical and tropical zones.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-000000000006', 'What were the three estates in 18th-century French society? Which estate paid all the taxes?', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Social Science', 'The French Revolution', 2, 'The three estates were: First Estate (Clergy), Second Estate (Nobility), and Third Estate (Big businessmen, merchants, court officials, lawyers, peasants, and landless artisans). Only the Third Estate paid all direct and indirect taxes (Taille and Tithe).', '1 Mark for listing the 3 estates correctly; 1 Mark for specifying that the Third Estate bore all taxes', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-000000000007', 'What is the ''Preamble'' to the Indian Constitution? State any two core democratic values enshrined in it.', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Social Science', 'Constitutional Design', 2, 'The Preamble is an introductory guiding statement that sets out the guiding purposes, principles, and philosophy of the Constitution. Core values: Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, Republic, Justice, Liberty, Equality, and Fraternity (any two).', '1 Mark for definition of Preamble; 1 Mark for mentioning two core values with brief context', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-000000000008', 'Explain any three major demands made by Vladimir Lenin in his famous ''April Theses'' of 1917.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Socialism in Europe and the Russian Revolution', 3, 'In April 1917, Bolshevik leader Vladimir Lenin returned to Russia and put forward three urgent demands known as April Theses: 1. The ongoing First World War must be brought to an immediate close. 2. All land owned by the nobility and clergy must be transferred to the peasants. 3. All banks must be nationalized under state control.', '1 Mark for end of World War I; 1 Mark for transfer of land to peasants; 1 Mark for nationalization of banks', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', 'Describe the three Himalayan river systems that form the northern plains of India and state two characteristics of their drainage.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Drainage', 3, 'The three river systems are: 1. The Indus River System, 2. The Ganga River System, 3. The Brahmaputra River System. Characteristics: (i) They are perennial rivers fed by both rainfall and melting Himalayan snow. (ii) In their upper courses, they perform intensive erosional action forming deep gorges, while in lower courses they create floodplains, meanders, and expansive deltas.', '1 Mark for naming the three river systems; 2 Marks for two distinct hydrological characteristics (perennial flow and depositional landforms)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003001f-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a', 'Describe the mechanism of the Indian Southwest Monsoon. Explain the role of the Inter-Tropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ), differential heating, and Tibetan plateau in triggering the monsoon.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'Social Science', 'Climate', 5, 'Mechanism: 1. Differential heating of land and sea: In summer, landmass of North India heats rapidly, creating low pressure, while surrounding oceans experience high pressure, pulling moisture-laden winds. 2. Shift of ITCZ: In summer, the ITCZ shifts northward over the Ganga plain, acting as the monsoon trough. 3. High pressure east of Madagascar: Presence of intense high pressure cell at ~20°S over the Indian Ocean directs powerful southeast trade winds across the equator toward India. 4. Tibetan Plateau: Intense heating of the Tibetan plateau results in strong vertical air currents and low pressure at 9 km elevation. 5. Jet Streams: Movement of the westerly jet stream to the north of Himalayas and presence of the tropical easterly jet stream over peninsular India.', '1 Mark each for 5 key physical atmospheric mechanisms triggering the Indian monsoon (total 5 Marks)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true)
