        ('9003002a-0000-4000-8000-000000000008', 'Explain any three major demands made by Vladimir Lenin in his famous ''April Theses'' of 1917.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Socialism in Europe and the Russian Revolution', 3, 'In April 1917, Bolshevik leader Vladimir Lenin returned to Russia and put forward three urgent demands known as April Theses: 1. The ongoing First World War must be brought to an immediate close. 2. All land owned by the nobility and clergy must be transferred to the peasants. 3. All banks must be nationalized under state control.', '1 Mark for end of World War I; 1 Mark for transfer of land to peasants; 1 Mark for nationalization of banks', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003002a-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', 'Describe the three Himalayan river systems that form the northern plains of India and state two characteristics of their drainage.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Drainage', 3, 'The three river systems are: 1. The Indus River System, 2. The Ganga River System, 3. The Brahmaputra River System. Characteristics: (i) They are perennial rivers fed by both rainfall and melting Himalayan snow. (ii) In their upper courses, they perform intensive erosional action forming deep gorges, while in lower courses they create floodplains, meanders, and expansive deltas.', '1 Mark for naming the three river systems; 2 Marks for two distinct hydrological characteristics (perennial flow and depositional landforms)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9003002a-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a', '(a) Differentiate between seasonal unemployment and disguised unemployment. (b) Describe the various government measures undertaken to reduce poverty in India under targeted anti-poverty programmes.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'Social Science', 'Poverty as a Challenge', 5, '(a) Distinctions: Seasonal unemployment occurs when people cannot find jobs during certain months of the year (e.g., farm labor during off-seasons). Disguised unemployment occurs when more workers are engaged in an activity than needed, with zero marginal productivity. (b) Targeted programmes: 1. MGNREGA 2005: Guarantees 100 days of manual wage employment per rural household. 2. PMGSY: Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana connecting rural habitations with all-weather roads. 3. PMRY / REGP: Providing subsidized financial assistance to educated unemployed youth for setting up micro-enterprises. 4. PDS & Antyodaya Anna Yojana: Highly subsidized grain distribution to the poorest families.', '2 Marks for unemployment differentiation; 3 Marks for comprehensive breakdown of targeted anti-poverty programmes', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true)
